Ahh I see, so the firmware actually does something like this (very pseudo-code)?
```
overscan_* = 0;
if (disable_overscan == 0) {
  overscan_* = 48, 32, 0; /* according to mode */
}
```

Mmm, @popcornmix, so to make things less confusing (for me), is this then what actually happens in the firmware (again very pseudo-code)?
```
internal_overscan_* = 0;
if (disable_overscan == 0) {
  internal_overscan = 48, 32, 0;  /* according to screen-mode */
}
internal_overscan_* += overscan_*;
```
